  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 239 PM CDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nThe next chance for storms arrives this weekend, likely late Friday \nnight and again Saturday night into Sunday. We are especially \nkeeping an eye on the rain Saturday and the potential for flooding. \nThe GFS is showing increasing PWATs throughout the day Saturday with \nvalues around 1.5-1.8 inches. The GFS is also showing that this will \nbe a slow moving system with the strong potential for backbuilding \nand training cells along the front which would result in locally \nhigher rainfall amounts. The risk of flooding is going to depend on \nhow much rain we see today and tomorrow but if we do see rain, the \npotential for flash flooding will increase on Saturday. As such, the \nWPC has issued a slight ERO for the western 2/3 of our CWA on \nSaturday. There is the potential for more storms Sunday night into \nMonday as models are depicting a surface low developing over the \nNorthern Plains but right now the heaviest rain should remain to our \nnorth.",
